            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SARAHGRACESC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed the recipe a bit. First I used flour tortillas. I used cheddar instead of mozz. I used green olives diced instead of black olives. I didn't have any avocados, so that was omitted. I used taco sauce instead of pepper sauce. And I added some black beans. I simply put the tortilla down on the hot (med heat) skillet, and put all of the fixings on that. Then I topped with the second tortilla and flipped it over, letting that side crisp up. They were delicious! I dipped in sour cream.",
